Yes. After reviewing `prx0r/finalbuilds2`, I think this is the cleanest interpretation:

> **FinalBuilds2 is already most of the scientific brain you need for Pogtown.**
>
> It should not generate the comedy itself. It should decide **what question to ask next, what evidence would discriminate between explanations, what experiment deserves another probe, and how belief should change after the result.**

Freaktown then becomes the experimental execution engine. Influence gets the experiment into the real world. qprivately controls consequences. Jev describes what happened. YouTube/Pogtown provide observations.

The major caveat is that FinalBuilds2 was originally specialized toward software/product ideas, so some of its abstractions transfer beautifully and some absolutely should **not** be reused unchanged.

