# One important correction: FinalBuilds2 does not yet contain the generalized Bayesian engine we ultimately want

There are actually two layers of thinking in the repository.

The older `HYPOTHESIS-CALIBRATION.md` proposes:

```text
Beta-Bernoulli
→ posterior updates
→ Thompson sampling
```

But the newer and better `HYPOTHESIS-EVOLUTION-POLICY.md` explicitly says:

> **Do not allocate builds by Beta-Bernoulli Thompson sampling over hypotheses.**

Instead it recommends:

```text
expected product utility
+ λ information gain
+ λ diversity
- build cost
- risk
```

and postpones full Bayesian optimal experimental design until the measurement layer works.

**The newer policy is right.**

For Pogtown, a single Beta posterior is nowhere near expressive enough.

Our outcomes include:

```text
CTR
early retention
retention AUC
completion
rewatches
shares
specific-positive-comment rate
character-positive-comment rate
return requests
subscriber effect
```

and our explanatory variables include:

```text
character
JokeBlock
topic
script realization
delivery
timing
gesture
mesh
camera
title
thumbnail
first frame
```

The eventual model wants to be hierarchical.

Conceptually:

```text
outcome
  ~ character
  + JokeBlock
  + topic
  + performance
  + visual
  + packaging
  + character×JokeBlock
  + character×performance
  + JokeBlock×topic
  + ...
```

So I would **keep the current forecast/calibration machinery**, but treat a proper hierarchical Bayesian model as a later inference backend.

Don't block MVP on PyMC-level machinery.

